The rewrite walks the vector with raw pointers instead of re-reading `size()` and indexing on every pass. That makes the loop body slightly cheaper. `GetNum()` is still called for every field, so the matching behaviour and the returned pointer are unchanged.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* p = fields.data();
    Field* const end = p + fields.size();
    for (; p != end; ++p)
    {
        if (p->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return p;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```